COSMIC Studio explicit single-event Iced message boundary

Original cosmic-panel b5cc19e351b82eed999097ced1ff267d27bf8e7a
cosmic-panel-bin/src/iced/state.rs is retained byte-exact in
pinned-iced-state.json.gz (original SHA256
199b3a9aa395a28fbc24f8007b9e472ccb0d9a591abda887d154689b5f9ec39a).
Original GPL-3.0 license text is pinned-keyboard-focus.LICENSE. This fixture,
new iced_keyboard_dispatch.rs and generator integration remain GPL-3.0-only;
repository MIT does not relicense them. Prior GPL/MPL and borrowed-Winit MIT
notices remain unchanged.

Explicit State::update_keyboard runs one converted keyboard event through the
actual Iced widget UI and carries its immutable original envelope to each
resulting message. Nonempty ordinary queues are refused without flushing or
relabeling. Validation and keyboard-only dispatch are mandatory explicit caller
arguments; no ordinary Program::update or first-seat pointer fallback occurs.
Validation precedes UI and each output. Returned tasks do not inherit context;
a later task output is ordinary untrusted work. No transactional rollback is
claimed after an earlier dispatcher changes live state.

No native keyboard callback or production wrapper invokes this method yet.
The synthetic widget tests use the real UI/cache/software renderer and original
safe converter, not actual WlSeat admission/keyboard/grab/recovery. A supplied
validator is not itself evidence of live seat/focus/target/modifier/order/press/
popup authorization. Those gates, deferred message authority, traversal and
restoration remain open. Hiding, configuration migration and deployment remain
disabled. No new dependency, unsafe code, timer or renderer trial.
